From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:41:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Lay a tabbed system grid out in columns that slide

- Theme variables esColumnPan, esColumnSlide and esColumnHeader
  (fractions of the screen) lay the tabbed home out as columns: at level 1
  the first column (the tabs) has the focus, up and down change the tab
  and the grid follows; right or A give the grid the focus and the view
  pans by the first column's width (360 ms, eased out, so it moves in the
  frame after the press); B or left at the grid's left edge pan back. The
  grid's cursor shows selected only at level 2, and {global:homeColumn}
  tells the theme the level shown, from the press.
- Right at the grid's right edge opens the system's games, as A does. The
  game list opens beside the home at level 2 and both slide left by
  esColumnSlide (eased out too); the column they share crossfades (the
  leaving view's elements over the first 35 % of the way, the coming
  one's from 30 to 70 %) while the backgrounds and the header band stay
  in place. B, or left at the game grid's left edge, slide back; L1/R1
  there slide back to the previous or next tab.
- An element's part comes from where the theme put it: full screen is the
  background, inside the header band stays in place, starting in the
  shared column fades, the rest slides. Without the variables, or with
  the power saver's instant mode, nothing changes.
- THEMES.md and THEMES_BINDINGS.md: the columns and {global:homeColumn}.
